! mcp_bootstrap_p343.strap -- MCP printed page 343: the $DUMP pump
! (APUMP5 .. APANEL): test the dump bounds against SPPLB/SMARK, branch
! to ADLWER, set up the print buffer (APCOL1, AMNMBF), write it
! (AWRITE), and the panel line routine (APANEL: "PANEL LINE 1"), lines
! 1-50.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.93, read at 400 dpi, doubtful glyphs
! at 900 dpi.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 22$DUMP  CARD
! ID VB000038  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 343"; the heading row's
! LOCATION field is 234733, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  50 lines; every line number prints a "*" after it.  One
! remark card (line 42, "- PANEL LINE 1"); no TAIL card on this page.
! Located rows run contiguous from 234733.00 (line 1) to 234771.40
! (line 50, V+I, a half word; next location 234772.00), then blank
! paper.  "*" after the LOCATION on lines 11, 30 and 50.
!
! JOIN.  p.342 and p.344 are not landed and have no scratch deck yet;
! line 1's location equals the heading-row LOCATION 234733 and the card
! ID VB000038 is line 1's serial.  p.344 should open at 234772.00 with
! serial VB000084.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * line 6 "CMOC00" = CM0000 (connective digits); its h2 prints
!     "011000.CC F0" = .00 (the drum prints 0 open).
!   * lines 16 and 22 "ACLWER" = ADLWER: the D prints with its stem
!     worn; lines 4 and 11 print it plainly D.  Line 7 "ACMPBG" =
!     ADMPBG and line 15's label "ADMPPR" read the same way (D worn;
!     line 9's BZXH,ADMPPR and line 14's ADMPND print the D plainly).
!   * line 31 APCOL1: the O is closed, the last glyph a flagged 1 (not
!     the barred I of ASPLBI); C22-6728 OCR reads "APCOLI", the ink
!     here says 1.
!   * line 40 AFORMT, line 41 AMNTOP: the O prints open ("AFCRMT",
!     "AMNTCP"); C22-6728 names AFORMT ("a B,AFORMT-.32") and AMNTOP
!     (the print buffer).  "NCP" = NOP.
!   * line 26 ALSRQ: the Q's tail prints.
!   * octal fields with an open round read 0.
!
! EXTERNALS.  SLRBU/SPPLB and SMARK are landed (p.116, p.103), forms
! copied from landed stand-ins.  Every other external is not landed;
! values from this page's binary (each comment says how much it fixes).
!
! CARD SERIALS.  VB000038 .. VB000083.  Shared serials: lines 32-33
! (VB000069), 35-36 (VB000071), 38-39 (VB000073), 46-47 (VB000080) --
! each a SIC,x / B,y pair.  None skipped.

SLRBU   SYN, (8)215324.0             ! landed p.116 line 21
SPPLB   SYN, SLRBU+.32               ! landed p.116 line 23
SMARK   SYN, (8)215012.40            ! landed; p.103 line 46 VF (form of p.293's stand-in)
ASPLBI  SYN, (8)236147.03            ! not landed; BZB1 line 3 / BB line 11 236147.03, BIT-EXACT
ASPUBI  SYN, (8)236147.02            ! not landed; BB line 4 / BZB1 line 10 236147.02, BIT-EXACT
ADLWER  SYN, (8)235231.0             ! not landed; BB line 4 h2 235231.34, half word only
ADMPBG  SYN, (8)236425.0             ! not landed; SVA line 7 236425.33, half word only
ADMPND  SYN, (8)236162.0             ! not landed; SVA line 14 236162.05, half word only
ALSRQ   SYN, (8)235221.40            ! not landed; BZB line 26 h2 235221.74, half word only
APUML7  SYN, (8)235226.0             ! not landed; LVI line 27 235226.11, half word only
APUML6  SYN, (8)234704.0             ! not landed; SVA line 28 234704.11, half word only
APUMP9  SYN, (8)234717.40            ! not landed; SVA line 30 234717.41, half word only
